{
  "_comment": "Hand-authored setup content. NOT generated -- the importers never touch this file. `presets` are named forces: a species and three army lists, kept because a test that wants a particular die on the board has to be able to say so, and because the golden corpus needs forces that never change. Terrain has no per-species profile any more (Phase 5b) -- both Home Terrains and the Frontier are drawn from the seed, from all 24 dice; see src/engine/setup.ts. The Treefolk and Firewalkers `_starter` lists are the 30-health ones the alpha shipped with (the goldens are recorded against them -- do not edit them), and the Coral Elves' and the Dwarves' follow their pattern die for die by class and size (v2 Phases 5f and 6h); the `_bestiary` lists are 35 health and hold one of every monster and every large die of their species, which is the widest SAI coverage a legal force can reach. The monster fixtures are one per monster die in the data -- six copies of that one monster, split 3/2/1 across home, Frontier and the enemy home. They exist so a rule about a monster face can be watched happening: six of one die against six of another is a game made of nothing but the two faces under test, where a bestiary buries the interesting die among nineteen others that may never roll. Six is what the setup cap allows -- 24 health, so no army may exceed 12, which is exactly the three at home. All are 24 health, so any two of them pair, mirrors included; none of them pairs with a starter (30) or a bestiary (35). An ordinary game rolls its forces from the seed instead.",
